The prescribed <orientation> orders the two edges from $A$ as $\mathbf c-\mathbf a$ followed by $\mathbf b-\mathbf a$. The <vector area> is half their <cross product>:
$$
\mathbf S=\frac12(\mathbf c-\mathbf a)\times(\mathbf b-\mathbf a)
=\frac12(-1,0,1)^T\times(-1,1,0)^T
=\boxed{-\frac12(1,1,1)^T}.
$$
The sign agrees with the <right-hand rule> for the traversal $A\to C\to B\to A$.

= b
{parent=1}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

For a constant <vector field>, the <flux integral> is its <dot product> with the <vector area>. Thus
$$
\Phi=\mathbf F\cdot\mathbf S
=(1,1,-1)\cdot\left(-\frac12,-\frac12,-\frac12\right)
=\boxed{-\frac12}.
$$

