= a
{parent=3}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=a}

Move the right-hand side to the left. The resulting <homogeneous linear system> has coefficient <matrix>
$$
\begin{pmatrix}-2&1\\1&b-2\end{pmatrix}.
$$
A nonzero solution exists exactly when its <determinant> vanishes:
$$
\boxed{(-2)(b-2)-1=0}.
$$
Here the upper-left entry of the original <matrix> is $-1$, as verified in the original PDF; that entry is corrupted in the local OCR.

= b
{parent=3}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

The <determinant> condition reduces to $3-2b=0$, giving
$$
\boxed{b=\frac32}.
$$
As a check, the first <linear equation> gives $y=2x$, and at this value of $b$ the second <linear equation> is satisfied for every such pair, including nonzero pairs.

= 4
{parent=Paper 2}
