An <eigenvalue> makes the shifted <matrix> singular, so its <characteristic polynomial> vanishes:
$$
\det\begin{pmatrix}1-\lambda&1\\1&2-\lambda\end{pmatrix}
=(1-\lambda)(2-\lambda)-1.
$$
Thus the <characteristic equation> is
$$
\boxed{\lambda^2-3\lambda+1=0}.
$$

= b
{parent=9}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

Applying the <quadratic formula> to the <characteristic polynomial> gives the two <eigenvalues>
$$
\boxed{\lambda=\frac{3+\sqrt5}{2}\quad\text{or}\quad\lambda=\frac{3-\sqrt5}{2}}.
$$

