= Solution
{parent=a}

The three tosses are <independent events>, each with head <probability> $1/2$. Consequently
$$
\boxed{\mathbb P(HHH)=\left(\frac12\right)^3=\frac18}.
$$

= b
{parent=10}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

The successful ordered outcomes are $TTH$, $THT$ and $HTT$. Each has <probability> $1/8$ by <independence>, and these <events> are <mutually exclusive events>[mutually exclusive]. Adding their <probabilities> gives
$$
\boxed{\mathbb P(\text{exactly two tails})=\frac38}.
$$
Equivalently, the <binomial distribution> gives $\binom32(1/2)^2(1/2)=3/8$.

